# ==============================================================================
#  Shivaayaha Silk Sarees — Environment Variables Quick Reference
#  Root: .env.example
#  ✅  This file IS committed to Git as a reference.
#
#  SETUP INSTRUCTIONS:
#    1. cp server/.env.example server/.env      ← server secrets
#    2. cp client/.env.example client/.env      ← frontend config
#    3. Edit both files with your real values
#    4. Never commit the actual .env files (already in .gitignore)
# ==============================================================================

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  BACKEND  →  server/.env
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  PORT                  Port Express listens on (default: 5000)
#  NODE_ENV              development | production | test
#  JWT_SECRET            64-char random hex — MUST change in production
#  JWT_EXPIRES_IN        Token TTL, e.g. 7d | 24h
#  DB_PATH               Path to SQLite file (default: ./shivaayaha.sqlite)
#  CORS_ORIGIN           Comma-separated list of allowed frontend origins
#  RATE_LIMIT_MAX        Max requests per window per IP (default: 100)
#  RATE_LIMIT_WINDOW_MS  Window duration in ms (default: 900000 = 15 min)
#  LOG_LEVEL             debug | info | warn | error

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  FRONTEND  →  client/.env
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  VITE_API_URL          Backend API base URL (default: /api for local dev)
#  VITE_APP_NAME         App display name
#  VITE_APP_VERSION      App version string
#  VITE_DEBUG_API        true | false — enables verbose API logging

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  GITHUB ACTIONS SECRETS  (for CI/CD deployment)
#  Add at: github.com/MuzamilMohammadK/Shivaayaha-Silk-Saree/settings/secrets/actions
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
#  ┌─────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
#  │ Secret Name         │ Value                                            │
#  ├─────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
#  │ EC2_HOST            │ Your EC2 public IP  (run: curl -s ifconfig.me)  │
#  │ EC2_USERNAME        │ ubuntu                                           │
#  │ SSH_PRIVATE_KEY     │ Full contents of Shivaayaha.pem key file         │
#  │ VITE_API_URL        │ http://YOUR-EC2-IP:5000/api                      │
#  └─────────────────────┴──────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  AWS EC2 DEPLOYMENT — STEP-BY-STEP CHECKLIST
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
#  PART A: Run inside EC2 terminal (ubuntu@YOUR-EC2-IP)
#  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
#  Step 1 — Install Node.js 22 + PM2:
#    curl -fsSL https://deb.nodesource.com/setup_22.x | sudo -E bash -
#    sudo apt install -y nodejs
#    sudo npm install -g pm2
#    pm2 startup        ← copy & run the command it prints
#
#  Step 2 — Get your public IP:
#    curl -s ifconfig.me
#
#  Step 3 — Create .env on EC2:
#    mkdir -p ~/shivaayaha-app/server
#    cat > ~/shivaayaha-app/server/.env << 'EOF'
#    NODE_ENV=production
#    PORT=5000
#    JWT_SECRET=<your-64-char-hex>
#    JWT_EXPIRES_IN=7d
#    DB_PATH=/home/ubuntu/shivaayaha-app/server/shivaayaha.sqlite
#    CORS_ORIGIN=https://muzamilmohammadk.github.io
#    LOG_LEVEL=info
#    EOF
#
#  Step 4 — Open port 5000 in AWS Security Group:
#    AWS Console → EC2 → Security Groups → Inbound Rules → Add Rule
#    Type: Custom TCP | Port: 5000 | Source: 0.0.0.0/0
#
#  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  PART B: Add GitHub Secrets (listed in table above)
#  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
#  PART C: Trigger First Deployment (run on local PC):
#    git commit --allow-empty -m "ci: trigger first EC2 backend deployment"
#    git push origin main
#    Then watch: GitHub → Actions tab → "Deploy Backend to AWS EC2" → ✅
#
#  PART D: Verify Backend is Running:
#    Open in browser: http://YOUR-EC2-IP:5000/api/health
#    Expected response: {"status":"ok","service":"Shivaayaha Silk Sarees Ledger API"}
#    ✅ Once this works, GitHub Pages frontend connects to backend automatically!
